dyanega@pop.ucr.edu (Doug Yanega) writes:
> I've never seen this mentioned as a possible "conduct" to keep track of.

It's been discussed several times before.

> Is there no way for the game to give you a special message when a pet that
> is ascending with you is your starting pet?

Currently not, since which monster _is_ your starting pet isn't kept
track of anywhere; you'd need to stuff its m_id into a variable that
gets saved with the game state (or add a monster flag, but that would
be silly for something that'll only ever be set on one monster). There
are other things to be considered; does polymorphing count?
Lifesaving?  Reviving? Retaming after it's gone wild?

(And conducts get shown at death as well as ascension; does a pet
count if it's anywhere on the level you die on? Within a certain
distance?)

(It's not a particularly _conductful_ thing, since you've got little
control over what mishaps may befall your pet; it's not something that
you can play towards. It's something that may be worth the game's
noting, that's all.)

